 "about": [
  "Akebono Shuzo is a brewery in Aizubange, in the Aizu region of Fukushima. It was founded in 1904, and its sixth-generation head took charge in 2013.",
  "In 1995 the brewery stopped using a visiting tōji and began brewing with a husband-and-wife team and local staff. Contract rice growing in Aizubange started in 1997, and Tenmei, now its core label, first appeared around the end of that decade.",
  "The 2011 earthquake destroyed three of its buildings. Since then it has planted wine grapes and obtained a licence to make fruit wine."
